        "math_academy_id": "q-161488",
        "problem": "Evaluate the mixed integral\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA\n$$\n\nwhere the region $D$ in the $xy$-plane is given by\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral with respect to $z,$ treating $x$ and $y$ as constants:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+y}}2z\\,dz]dA & ={\u222c}_{D}[{z}^{2}]_{z=0}^{z=\\sqrt{x+y}}\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}({(\\sqrt{x+y})}^{2}-0)\\,dA \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}x+y\\,dA\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the double integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}x+y\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}x+y\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[xy+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{2}]}_{y=0}^{y={x}^{2}}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{2}({x}^{4}-0)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{4}\\,dx \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{10}{x}^{5}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{10}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
